iffs","r":"management","s":"Max Mitchell","x":"We are effectively managing the current tariff and inflation headwinds and we expect to be able to offset all impacts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/23/crane-co-cr-q3-2018-earnings-conference-call-trans.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2018 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2018-10-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Richard Maue","x":"We continue to believe that we will be able to offset any incremental pressure from tariffs or commodity costs and we are still on track to achieve our original guidance of 13% adjusted operating margins in this segment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/23/crane-co-cr-q3-2018-earnings-conference-call-trans.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2018 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2018-10-23","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Richard Maue","x":"The increased guidance primarily reflects incremental strength at Aerospace & Electronics and Crane Currency along with modestly lower interest expense and a slightly lower than expected tax rate.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/23/crane-co-cr-q3-2018-earnings-conference-call-trans.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2018 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2019-01-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Drew Haroldson","x":"Could you provide a quick update to the tariff impact in 2019?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/29/crane-co-cr-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-trans.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2018 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2019-01-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"We are planning for tariffs to hit us a bit, but we feel very confident that we will be able to offset that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/29/crane-co-cr-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-trans.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2018 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2019-01-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Damian Karas","x":"I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/29/crane-co-cr-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-trans.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2019-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Nate Jones","x":"I guess fair enough I'll pass it on thanks.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/30/crane-co-cr-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2019-07-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"Yes, so overall, -- we've been doing -- the teams have been doing a fantastic job on on price cost, dealing with the tariff exposures that we have as well as the dynamic movements on material cost.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/23/crane-co-cr-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2019-07-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Nathan Jones","x":"Okay, I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/23/crane-co-cr-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2019-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Richard Maue","x":"I'll pass it on.Thanks, Nathan.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/29/crane-co-cr-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2019-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max Mitchell","x":"The policy changes refer to cost reduction efforts by the depository institutions which have had the net effect of keeping notes in circulation longer.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/29/crane-co-cr-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2020-01-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Robert Barry","x":"I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/28/crane-co-cr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2020-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"No, we're not planning any cost reduction initiatives, Ken.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/28/crane-co-cr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2019 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2020-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Brett Linzey","x":"So the $10 million of incremental restructuring you're doing, how does that feather in over the next couple of years?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/28/crane-co-cr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2020-04-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Nathan Jones","x":"I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/28/crane-co-cr-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2020-04-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"That EPS forecast includes incremental cost savings of at least $100 million this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/28/crane-co-cr-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2020-04-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"I mentioned earlier that our guidance assumes $100 million of gross realized cost savings in 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/28/crane-co-cr-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2020-07-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Nathan Jones","x":"I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/28/crane-co-cr-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2020-07-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"Rich is going to provide an update on liquidity as well as details on our specific cost reduction measures to date.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/28/crane-co-cr-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2020-07-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"Based on this, we are narrowing our EPS guidance range for full year 2020 to $3.30 to $4.10, which reflects a core sales decline of 17% to 21% and incremental gross cost savings of at least $100 million this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/28/crane-co-cr-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2020-10-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"We continue to expect incremental gross cost savings of at least $100 million this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/27/crane-co-cr-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2020-10-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"From a cost perspective, we are on track to modestly exceed our target of $100 million in gross realized cost savings in 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/27/crane-co-cr-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2021-01-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"And our plans for 2021 incorporate the right level of pass-through on price.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/26/crane-co-cr-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2021-01-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Nathan Jones","x":"Can you talk about how that likely impacts your ability to pass through higher raw materials?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/26/crane-co-cr-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2021-01-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"We were able to accomplish this solid performance, in part, because of our thoughtful and decisive action on cost reduction measures, but it also reflects years of work operationally to ensure that our footprint is appropriately sized and flexible enough to quickly adapt to sharp changes in demand.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/26/crane-co-cr-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2020 Q4","e":"cr","d":"2021-01-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"First, we knew we needed to take quick -- we needed to act quickly on cost reductions, given the 2020 demand outlook, and we delivered $105 million of gross cost savings last year, an impressive figure for our cost base, particularly since we intentionally didn't execute on most actions until May.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/26/crane-co-cr-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2021-05-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Matt J. Summerville","x":"Can you talk about what you're seeing in terms of price realization year-over-year, whether you need to go get more price in that business to help offset inflation?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/crane-co-cr-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2021-05-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"However, this sale was directly enabled by our ongoing restructuring efforts as we moved operations from this facility to other locations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/crane-co-cr-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2021-05-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"Since 2017, we have received proceeds from real estate and other asset sales made possible by restructuring activities of approximately $47 million, which means that much of our restructuring has actually been self-funded.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/crane-co-cr-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2021-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Damian Karas","x":"I will pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/27/crane-co-cr-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2021-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max Mitchell","x":"Message is the same, execution on our growth initiatives, together with the consistent cadence and discipline of the Crane Business System to drive growth, productivity and cost savings.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/27/crane-co-cr-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2021-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Rich Maue","x":"However, one of these sales was directly enabled by our ongoing restructuring efforts as we moved operations from this facility to other locations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/27/crane-co-cr-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2021-07-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Rich Maue","x":"That means we have effectively raised guidance about $1.50 on an operational basis since the beginning of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/27/crane-co-cr-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2021-10-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"We are executing on numerous growth initiatives across our businesses and we operate with a consistent cadence and discipline of the Crane Business System to drive growth, productivity, and cost savings.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/26/crane-co-cr-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2021-10-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"The higher corporate costs reflect a number of factors including a charge related to a foreign pension plan that we are restructuring and a higher professional service cost level particularly legal costs related to M&A due diligence and other matters.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/26/crane-co-cr-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2021 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2021-10-26","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Max H. Mitchell","x":"That means we have effectively raised guidance more than $1.80 on a comparable basis since January.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/26/crane-co-cr-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2024 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2024-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Max Mitchell","x":"You're taking cost out.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q3-2024-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2024 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2024-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Max Mitchell","x":"So it's not just a price up, it's a cost out.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q3-2024-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2024 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2024-10-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Rich Maue","x":"For the quarter, our results included about $0.03 of EPS impact for both those sites and our raised outlook includes an estimated $0.05 to $0.10 impact from production downtime in Q4.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q3-2024-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2024 Q3","e":"cr","d":"2024-10-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Rich Maue","x":"We raised guidance for the third consecutive quarter, full year sales growth up 11%, with segment margins expanding 140 basis points to 21% and EPS growth of 19%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q3-2024-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2025 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2025-04-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Alex Alcala","x":"Before I get into the segments, let me provide some insights into our tariff exposure.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q1-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2025 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2025-04-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Alex Alcala","x":"Overall, about 7% to 8% of our cost of goods sold consists of materials and components that are directly imported into the United States, another 3% to 4% of cost of goods sold are intercompany sales into United States, a portion of which is exempt from tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q1-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2025 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2025-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Nathan Jones","x":"I guess the question there is, do you think customers were prepositioning ahead of tariff-related price increases?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q1-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2025 Q1","e":"cr","d":"2025-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Scott Deuschle","x":"I’ll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/26/crane-cr-q1-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2025 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2025-07-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"…one times net debt to EBITDA, still below our two to three times targeted range, leaving us well-positioned for further M&A. With respect to tariffs, as a reminder, only about 7% to 8% of our cost of goods sold consist of materials and components that are directly imported into the United States.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/04/crane-cr-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2025 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2025-07-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"Another three to 4% of cost of goods sold are intercompany sales into the United States, a portion of which is exempt from tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/04/crane-cr-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CR 2025 Q2","e":"cr","d":"2025-07-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Richard A. Maue","x":"For the full year, as Max noted, we are raising our outlook to a range of $5.5 to $5.8.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcr